<title>UK: Nat Grid, Nat Power win pensions ruling.</title>
<headline>Nat Grid, Nat Power win pensions ruling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British court on Tuesday ruled in favour of electricity supply company National Grid and utility National Power Plc over their use of pensions surpluses to fund redundancy payments.</p>
<p>Mr Justice Robert Walker allowed an appeal by National Grid against a decision by Britain's pensions ombudsman that it should return 43 million stg.</p>
<p>He also ruled that the arrangements made by National Power had been valid and effective.</p>
</text>
